sequenceDiagram
    actor S1 as Support (tab 1)
    actor S2 as Support (tab 2)
    participant N as IpService.move
    participant DB as MySQL

    S1->>N: move(ip, from = A, to = B)
    S2->>N: move(ip, from = A, to = C)
    N->>DB: BEGIN, SELECT ip FOR UPDATE (tab 1 gets the lock)
    Note over N,DB: tab 2 waits here
    N->>DB: open assignment is on A? yes
    N->>DB: lock target server B, must be pending/running
    N->>DB: A keeps at least one other address?
    N->>DB: UPDATE old assignment: ended_at = clock
    N->>DB: INSERT assignment on B, started_at = same clock value
    N->>DB: COMMIT
    N->>DB: (tab 2) SELECT ip FOR UPDATE, open assignment is on B, not A
    N-->>S2: IpMoveRefused "no longer on that server"
    Note over DB: without the lock the unique index on<br/>open_ip_id still refuses a second open assignment
